---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Header, Footer } from '../components/ui';
import '../styles/business.css';
import { emailPasswordEnabled, authEmailsEnabled } from '../lib/auth';
---
<Base title="Restore your lifetime access | MinimalPairs" description="Information for existing MinimalPairs lifetime customers during the rebuild." noindex>
  <Header /><main class="editorial-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FOR OUR EXISTING CUSTOMERS</p><h1>Your purchase still counts.</h1><p class="editorial-lede">Your original lifetime purchase still covers all current and future language trainers.</p><section><h2>Use your original purchase email.</h2><p>Use the email on your original purchase receipt. If you previously signed in with Google, keep using that same Google account. We match your verified email to the original paid purchase, and your account shows when lifetime access is connected. You do not need to buy it again.</p><p>{emailPasswordEnabled && authEmailsEnabled ? "If your receipt email is not connected to Google, create an email and password account, then explicitly request and complete email verification. If you already have an account on this rebuilt site, sign in or request a password reset instead. Verification allows us to check the preserved purchase; it does not create a purchase." : "If your purchase email is not connected to Google, your entitlement is still preserved. Email sign-in and verification recovery are being prepared and are not fully available yet. No recovery message is sent by opening this page. The starter exercises remain open without signing in."}</p><a href="/account#membership" class="button button-dark">Sign in to restore access →</a></section><section><h2>Keep your existing account.</h2><p>A Google sign-in and an email password can belong to the same account. If you already use Google, sign in with Google first; when email sign-in is enabled, you can explicitly add a password to that account. We do not automatically merge or delete accounts. If a password is forgotten, a reset changes the password without replacing the account identity or its saved history.</p><p>Purchases stay unavailable to unverified emails. After following a verification link, return to your account and choose “I’ve verified my email” to refresh verification and check access.</p></section><section><h2>Your previous practice history</h2><p>Your purchase and your practice history are separate. Purchased access has been preserved; older passwords and practice records have not been transferred. New guest sessions are saved in this browser.</p></section></main><Footer />
</Base>
